  - id: the_pur_the_lot
    displayName: The Pur (the Lot)
    flavorText: Mordecai and Esther establish the annual feast of Purim, named for
      the lot Haman cast to set the date of the Jews' destruction, turning that day
      into a lasting celebration of deliverance.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: Establishes an annual two-day feast (the 14th and 15th of Adar) commemorating
      the Jews' deliverance from Haman's planned massacre, turning mourning into
      a lasting memorial kept in every generation, family, province, and city. Named
      Purim after the Pur (lot) Haman cast to set the date of destruction, so the
      instrument of the intended destruction becomes the name of the celebrated deliverance
      instead.
